      "explain": "To go from <strong>decimal to any base</strong>, divide repeatedly by that base and read the remainders <strong>bottom to top</strong>. To go from <strong>any base to decimal</strong>, multiply each digit by its positional weight and add. Between binary, octal and hexadecimal, you never touch decimal at all — you just <strong>group the bits</strong>: 3 bits per octal digit, 4 bits per hex digit.",
