      "subtopics": [
        {
          "title": "Signed magnitude versus 2's complement",
          "text": "Signed magnitude is the obvious idea: use one bit for the sign and the rest for the size. It is easy for humans to read, but bad for hardware — it needs two separate circuits (one for add, one for subtract), and it wastes a pattern on a useless second zero. 2's complement fixes both problems, which is why every modern processor uses it."
