      "subtopics": [
        {
          "title": "BCD is NOT the same as binary",
          "text": "Pure binary 45 is 101101 — six bits, one single number. BCD 45 is 0100 0101 — eight bits, two separate digits glued together. They look similar but are completely different. BCD wastes space, but it makes driving a seven-segment display or printing a decimal number trivially easy, which is why calculators and digital meters use it."
        },
        {
          "title": "Why Excess-3 is 'self-complementing'",
